Implement user story SKY-004-B: Dashboard HTML and build configuration

## Story Description
Create src/public/index.html as a styled single-page dashboard with search form and client-side JS. Configure package.json with start/build scripts, ensure build copies static assets to dist/public/, and add supertest devDependencies. Depends on SKY-004-A for the server that serves this file.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/public/index.html has a full-width blue (#1a73e8) header bar with bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and subtitle line below it
- Dashboard contains a centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, padding) with 2-column grid: From/To text inputs (row 1), Date/Adults inputs (row 2), each with label above the input
- Dashboard has a full-width blue search button (same color as header) and status area: pink/red banner for errors, gray text for empty results, count on success
- Client-side JS submits form via GET /search (no page reload), disables button during request, renders flights into results table in the same page
- package.json has 'start' script ('node dist/server.js') and 'build' script that produces dist/server.js and copies src/public/ to dist/public/; after `npm run build && npm run start`, dist/public/index.html exists, GET / serves the dashboard, and GET /health returns 200
- supertest and @types/supertest listed in devDependencies; `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0





